.TH HEDIT 1 "2026-09-16" "hedit 0.21.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hedit \- a lightweight terminal-based text editor written in hica
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hedit
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.RB [ + LINE [: COL ]]
.RI [ FILE ]
.br
.B hedit
.RB ( \-\-help | \-\-version )
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hedit
is a terminal text editor that pairs familiar, readline-style editing
with a small Lisp-based configuration and plugin language called
\fBHiLisp\fR. It supports multiple buffers, split panes, mouse input,
multi-cursor editing, incremental search, and a branching visual undo
tree.
.PP
With no
.I FILE
argument,
.B hedit
opens a single empty scratch buffer. If
.I FILE
does not exist yet, it is created in memory and only written to disk
on the first save.
.PP
All configuration \(em settings, key bindings, and plugins \(em is
loaded from a single
.B init.hl
file written in HiLisp; see
.B CONFIGURATION
below.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI + LINE
Move the cursor to
.I LINE
(1-indexed) after opening
.IR FILE .
.TP
.BI + LINE : COL
Move the cursor to
.I LINE
and column
.I COL
(both 1-indexed) after opening
.IR FILE .
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-readonly
Open
.I FILE
in read-only mode. Save
.RB ( Ctrl-s )
is disabled for the session.
.TP
.BI \-\-tabsize\ N
Override the configured tab size for this run. Takes precedence over
any
.RI "(set \(lqtabsize\(rq ...)"
form in
.BR init.hl .
.TP
.BI \-c\ PATH ", " \-\-config\ PATH
Load configuration from
.I PATH
instead of using the default search order (see
.B FILES
below).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-config
Skip loading a user
.B init.hl
entirely and run with built-in defaults.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a short usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the
.B hedit
version and exit.
.PP
The
.BI + LINE [: COL ]
form is a bare positional token (no leading option name) and may
appear before or after
.IR FILE .
Command-line flags always take precedence over an equivalent
.B init.hl
setting.
.SH KEY BINDINGS
Almost every binding below can be remapped from
.B init.hl
with
.RI ( bind
.RB \*(lq KEYSTROKE \*(rq
.RI \*(aq ACTION \*(aq )\c
; arrow keys, Enter, Backspace, and Esc are fixed. Press
.B Ctrl-g
inside
.B hedit
at any time for a live overlay of the currently active bindings,
generated straight from the running configuration.
.SS File operations
.TP
.B Ctrl-s
Save the current buffer. On a pathless (scratch) buffer this opens
the Save-As prompt instead.
.TP
.B Ctrl-o
Open the "open file" prompt.
.TP
.B Ctrl-q
Quit. With two or more panes open, closes the active pane and its
buffer instead, and only exits
.B hedit
once a single pane remains.
.SS Cursor & line editing (readline-style)
.TP
.B Ctrl-a\fR\ /\ \fBCtrl-e
Move to the start / end of the current line.
.TP
.B Meta-f\fR\ /\ \fBMeta-b
Move forward / back one word.
.TP
.B Ctrl-d
Delete the character under the cursor (forward-delete).
.TP
.B Ctrl-k
Kill from the cursor to the end of the line, into the clipboard.
.TP
.B Ctrl-w
Kill the word before the cursor, into the clipboard.
.TP
.B Meta-d
Kill the word after the cursor, into the clipboard.
.TP
.B Meta-l
Kill the entire current line, into the clipboard.
.TP
.B Ctrl-c\fR\ /\ \fBCtrl-v
Copy / paste. With an active selection, copy/replace just the
selected text instead of the whole line.
.TP
.B Ctrl-y
Yank \(em same clipboard slot as
.BR Ctrl-v .
.TP
.B Ctrl-z\fR\ /\ \fBCtrl-r
Undo / redo.
.SS Selections
.TP
.B Ctrl-Space
Set or clear the mark at the cursor.
.TP
.B Arrow keys
With a mark set, extend the selection to the new cursor position.
.TP
.B Meta-a
Select the entire buffer.
.SS Multi-cursor editing
.TP
.B Meta-c
Add a cursor at the next occurrence of the word under the cursor (or
the active selection); selects the word on the first press, adds the
next match on repeat.
.TP
.B Meta-click
Add an extra cursor at the mouse click position.
.TP
.B Esc
Collapse all cursors back to a single cursor and clear selections.
.PP
Typing, deleting, and pasting apply simultaneously at every active
cursor.
.SS Branching undo tree
.TP
.B Meta-t
Toggle a full-screen Unicode undo-tree overlay with a live preview of
each revision.
.TP
.B Meta-u
Cycle sibling branches in the undo graph.
.PP
Inside the undo tree overlay:
.B Up/Down
(or
.BR k / j )
navigate revisions,
.B Enter
restores the selected revision, and
.B Esc
cancels.
.SS Find
.TP
.B Ctrl-f
Open the find bar. Matches highlight live as you type.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Right\fR\ /\ \fBCtrl-Left
Jump to the next / previous match, wrapping at either end.
.TP
.B Enter
Close the find bar and jump to the next match; the search stays
active.
.TP
.B Esc
Cancel and drop the search, clearing highlights.
.PP
Search is plain-substring, case-sensitive, and whole-buffer.
.SS Buffers
.B hedit
keeps open buffers in a ring rather than a tab bar.
.TP
.B Meta-o
Open a new scratch buffer, pushing the current one onto the ring.
.TP
.B Meta-n\fR\ /\ \fBMeta-p
Switch to the next / previous buffer in the ring.
.TP
.B Meta-w
Close the active buffer (refuses to close the last remaining one).
.SS Split panes
.TP
.B Meta-v\fR\ /\ \fBMeta-h
Open a vertical / horizontal split prompt. Type a path and press
Enter to open that file in the new pane, or press Enter on an empty
prompt to duplicate the current buffer.
.TP
.B Meta-Arrows
Move focus to the nearest pane in that direction.
.TP
.B Meta-Tab
Cycle focus to the next pane.
.PP
A divider can be dragged with the mouse to resize the adjacent panes.
.SS Mouse
Click to place the cursor, drag to select, click or drag a pane
divider to resize, and scroll to move the viewport. Modifier-held
clicks (Ctrl/Option) are not currently decoded.
.SS Help & configuration
.TP
.B Ctrl-g
Toggle the keybindings overlay.
.TP
.B Meta-r
Reload
.B init.hl
and plugins live, without restarting.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B hedit
is configured entirely through a HiLisp file named
.BR init.hl .
HiLisp is a small Lisp dialect; see
.B FILES
below for where
.B hedit
looks for it.
.PP
Three built-ins cover the whole surface:
.TP
.BI "(set " key " " value )
Set a configuration value, e.g.
.RI "(set \*(lqtabsize\*(rq 4)" .
.TP
.BI "(get " key )
Read back a previously set configuration value.
.TP
.BI "(bind " keystroke " " action )
Map a keystroke (e.g.
.RI \*(lq Ctrl-s \*(rq )
to a named action (e.g.
.IR 'save ).
.RI \*(aq ignore \*(aq
silences a default binding without replacing it.
.PP
A syntax or runtime error in
.B init.hl
does not lock the editor out: it is evaluated top to bottom, stops at
the first error, surfaces it in the status line, and keeps whatever
loaded successfully before that point.
.PP
An annotated example covering every available setting and action name
ships at
.IR examples/init.hl " in the hedit source tree."
.SH PLUGINS
Plugins are ordinary HiLisp files loaded by opt-in name from
.B init.hl
via
.RI "(plugin \*(lq" name "\*(rq)" ,
which resolves to
.IR name /plugin.hl
in a
.B plugins
directory next to whichever
.B init.hl
was actually loaded.
.PP
A plugin registers callbacks with
.RI "(on '" event " (fn (...) ...))"
for lifecycle events:
.BR buffer-open ", " pre-save ", " post-save ", " pre-action ", and " quit .
If a
.B pre-save
or
.B pre-action
hook returns false, the save or action is skipped (the
.B quit
action can never be trapped this way). If a hook returns a string, it
is shown as the next status-bar message.
.PP
See
.IR examples/plugins/ " in the hedit source tree for reference plugins."
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/hedit/init.hl
Primary configuration file (falls back to
.IR $HOME/.config/hedit/init.hl
if
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset).
.TP
.I $HOME/.hedit.hl
Used if neither of the above exists.
.PP
The first file found in that order wins; if none exist,
.B hedit
runs with built-in defaults. A
.B \-\-config
argument or
.B \-\-no\-config
flag overrides this search entirely.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B hedit
Open an empty scratch buffer.
.TP
.B hedit notes.txt
Open
.IR notes.txt .
.TP
.B hedit +42:8 notes.txt
Open
.I notes.txt
with the cursor at line 42, column 8.
.TP
.B hedit \-R /etc/hosts
Open a file read-only.
.TP
.B hedit \-\-config ~/dotfiles/hedit-init.hl notes.txt
Load configuration from a non-default path.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B hedit
exits 0 on a normal quit
.RB ( Ctrl-q ).
A non-zero status indicates a startup failure such as an unreadable
file argument.
.SH BUGS
Windows is not supported. Modifier-held mouse clicks (Ctrl/Option)
are not decoded. Report issues at
.BR https://github.com/cladam/hedit/issues .
.SH SEE ALSO
Full keybinding reference:
.I docs/hedit-cheatsheet.md
in the hedit source tree.
.PP
